  "text": "Watch the ending you are trying. Choose Use this ending to select these words for Sol.\n\nThe last boat returned, and Mara helped its passengers ashore before leaving the dock.\n\nPip holds the chosen picture. Move it to the lantern and release to keep this memory.\n\nPip reads Mara’s story while Mara works. Afterward, he takes Grandma’s story to Mara.\n\nYour latest changes haven't been saved yet. Keep this page open and try saving again.\n\nMara has finished helping the passengers. Let Sol bring his manuscript to the garden.\n\nThis saved adventure belongs to a different content version. It has been kept safely.\n\nGrandma has finished her own story. The first part describes the garden before today.\n\nRecord and listen back here. This demo keeps your recording in this practice window.\n\nThe first section is secure. Walk onto it, then place and secure the second section.\n\nPip takes Grandma’s two repair ropes. Fasten one end of the footbridge to each bank.\n\nPip takes the same seed out of the boat. You can carry it across the bridge instead.\n\nTell Grandma what Sol wants to share, then agree a gathering time with your friends.\n\nGrandma is returning to the planting spot. You can plant together when she arrives.\n\nSol is helping Rina at the bakery. Follow the path to the right, past his workshop.\n\nGrandma holds the seed and walks back to the planting spot. Pip can keep exploring.\n\nMara asks, “Would you like some help?” The boy hesitates, then holds out the bird.\n\nRina’s repaired roof keeps the flour dry. She bakes bread. Rain continues outside.\n\nThe boat is alongside. Help the last passengers ashore before Mara can leave work.\n\nLoop plays the whole story. Pause, replay or open the full text with reading help.\n\nThe water is too deep to walk through. Stay on the bank or the finished crossing.",
